# {{projectName}}

Django (Python) project scaffolded by InitPad, served by gunicorn.

- Local: `pip install -r requirements.txt` then `python manage.py runserver`
- Routes: `GET /` and `GET /health`

Direct dependencies live in `requirements.in`; `requirements.txt` pins them
together with every transitive package, so each build installs the same
versions. After changing `requirements.in`, regenerate the lock with
`pip install pip-tools` and `pip-compile requirements.in`.

Every start without `DJANGO_SECRET_KEY` uses a new random key, so no key is
baked into the image. Set a persistent `DJANGO_SECRET_KEY` through InitPad's
environment secrets before storing sessions or other signed data. Generate one
with `python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(50))"`. To accept
only known host names, set `DJANGO_ALLOWED_HOSTS` (comma-separated).
